--- body ---

## Context

Child of 0700. A deterministic prefilter, run before any model call, that considers only pool records carrying the DataCite mandatory metadata: identifier, creator, title, publisher, publicationYear, resourceType. Term of art: a minimum metadata profile (a Dublin Core application profile); the DataCite mandatory fields are the cited reference.

Author-decided: the full six-field set; works lacking author, title, year or a handle are not worth screening; Handle means a DOI, an OpenAlex id, a RePEc, OAI, HAL or hdl handle, or a persistent id on a registered repository platform with a resolvable URL (redalyc, garuda, clacso, ipea and similar). Excluded records stay in the pool with their reason (single-standard rule), counted in the PRISMA flow, never deleted.

Evidence from the read-only counts of 2026-10-09 (lane deliveries, record-level, not the real pool; the pool grew with 1654 round 1, about 208k works):
- t1810 RePEc: the four-field gate drops 330 of 79,522; the full set 332. Undated records are 329, mostly chapters (184 of 1,806).
- Across the nine lane deliveries (sum 417,263, overlapping): four fields (without author, unmeasurable there) 15,331; full set 28,414. The extra 13,083 are almost all a missing publisher proxy (journal or ISSN) on OpenAlex book chapters, conference papers, dissertations, reports, preprints and books, caused by the ingester (2041), not by the works.
- Of the identifier drops, 2,231 per t1652 run are RePEc handles hidden in EDS accession numbers (2040) and t1653's 5.7k are repository ids and handles the first test did not recognise.

MOE note, author decision stands: a mandatory publisher overlaps the venue facet (2042), where an unknown publisher scores 0.5 rather than excluding. The author chose the full set; this ticket therefore makes publisher resolution a real step (host organization from 2041, then the DOI-prefix registrant on a publisher list, platform prefixes such as SSRN, Zenodo and Figshare not counted as publishers) and reports what the requirement costs so the choice can be revisited by evidence.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The profile is declared in one config block (mandatory fields, accepted identifier forms, registered platforms, publisher resolution order) with a version.
- [ ] Publisher resolution: OpenAlex host organization first, then the DOI-prefix registrant if its prefix is on a publisher list (Crossref prefix lookup; DataCite prefixes checked for coverage), else unresolved. Platform prefixes stay unresolved.
- [ ] Positive control before any count: known works with and without each field fail and pass as expected, including a chapter whose publisher comes only from the DOI prefix.
- [ ] Counts on the real pool (after `make rel-pool-data` and with 1654 round 1 stated as merged or not), by lane, period (1990-2006, 2007-2014, 2015-2025), language and doc type, with the drop reason per field. The first act and non-English share are reported separately before the filter is applied.
- [ ] Excluded records keep a reason code (`profile_missing_<field>`), stay in the pool and are tallied in `rel_counts.json`; no work is deleted.
- [ ] The filter is a switch in the existing sensitivity machinery: counts are reported with the publisher requirement on and off.
- [ ] The filter runs before stage 1 and stage 2 model calls; the spend avoided is derived and shown.
- [ ] Diff at most 14 content-bearing paths; scoped gate quoted (`selected:` and `skipped:`).

## Notes

Blocked by 2040 and 2041 because gating before the ingesters are fixed would drop real works for harvest artifacts. Overlaps to check before starting: 1654 (citation chaining, unmerged, its collector keeps authors), 2028 and 2029 (occurrence quarantine, open PR #1718, which touches `config/rel_screen.yaml`, `docs/rel-intake-contract.md`, `scripts/corpus_rel_repec_prefilter.py`, `scripts/corpus_rel_view.py` and `scripts/corpus_icf_stage1_input.py`, the files this prefilter will most likely edit), 2010 (three-facet instrument, merged). Open a coordination change first if three or more sessions end up on one of those files.
